 - `Organization` uses `PROTECT` on its venue FK — you must remove all venues before deleting an organization.
 - `ConditionReading.update_piano_current_state()` copies readings to denormalized fields on Piano for fast display.
 - `Piano.advance_schedule(task_type, completed_date)` computes the next due date when a work order is completed.
+
+---
+
+## Postgres Deployment
+
+This project is configured to use Postgres when `DATABASE_URL` is set and SQLite locally when it is not.
+
+Required production environment variables:
+
+```bash
+SECRET_KEY=your-real-secret-key
+DEBUG=False
+ALLOWED_HOSTS=your-app-name.onrender.com,yourdomain.com
+CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS=https://your-app-name.onrender.com,https://yourdomain.com
+DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DBNAME
+DB_SSL_REQUIRE=True
+```
+
+Typical deploy commands:
+
+```bash
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+python manage.py collectstatic --noinput
+python manage.py migrate
+```
+
+Typical web start command:
+
+```bash
+gunicorn piano_maintainer.wsgi:application
+```
+
+### Moving existing SQLite data into Postgres
+
+From your local SQLite database:
+
+```bash
+python manage.py dumpdata --exclude auth.permission --exclude contenttypes > data.json
+```
+
+After setting `DATABASE_URL` to your Postgres database:
+
+```bash
+python manage.py migrate
+python manage.py loaddata data.json
+```
+
+Do not commit `db.sqlite3`, `.env`, or production secrets.
